* bench_opamp: single-pole voltage-feedback op-amp (project-authored, textbook topology).
* Ports: inp inn out. Output referenced to ground (no supply pins, no rails).
* A: DC open-loop gain (V/V). GBW: gain-bandwidth product (Hz); the pole sits at GBW/A.
* ROUT: output resistance (ohm). 1 Tohm from each input to ground keeps an input that is
* driven only through a capacitor solvable; it is negligible against any real source.
.subckt bench_opamp inp inn out params: A=100k GBW=1meg ROUT=1
Rinp inp 0 1e12
Rinn inn 0 1e12
Egain n1 0 inp inn {A}
Rpole n1 n2 1k
Cpole n2 0 {A/(6.283185307179586*GBW*1k)}
Ebuf n3 0 n2 0 1
Rout n3 out {ROUT}
.ends bench_opamp
